{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 100)` priors for `sigma_a1`, `sigma_a2`, and `sigma_y`. These parameters already had finite bounds `<lower=0, upper=100>` in the original model, so the added priors are the matching proper uniform priors on the existing constrained support and satisfy SafeStan's requirement that every parameter have exactly one built-in prior before use. The observation model `y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y)` is unchanged, and `N`, `county`, and `x` remain unprotected context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=85> county;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[85] a1;
  vector[85] a2;
  real mu_a1;
  real mu_a2;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a1;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a2;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a1[county[i]] + a2[county[i]] * x[i];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a1 ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a1 ~ uniform(0, 100);
  a1 ~ normal(mu_a1, sigma_a1);
  mu_a2 ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a2 ~ uniform(0, 100);
  a2 ~ normal(0.1 * mu_a2, sigma_a2);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);

  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":1,"county":[1],"x":[4.278181375128752],"y":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
